{"availability":"available","full":"doppler-dsp/doppler","name":"doppler","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-21T19:37:48Z","updated":"2026-10-10T15:02:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://doppler-dsp.github.io/doppler/","topics":[],"demo":"https://doppler-dsp.github.io/doppler/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.813Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.813Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.813Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.813Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Practical, portable, performant digital signal processing.","doppler is a C99 DSP library — NCO, FIR, FFT, polyphase resampling, DDC, AGC, carrier and burst acquisition, DSSS receivers, convolutional and Reed-Solomon coding, CCSDS framing and more — with file, buffer, and NATS-based streaming, and a scenario-driven waveform generator (wfmgen) with byte-identical CLI/Python/C parity. Python and Rust wrap the same C core — no second implementation, no divergence, full SIMD throughput from any language.","New here? Start with Start Here — a one-page map from \"what are you trying to do\" to the right doc."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/doppler-dsp/doppler/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"42b2529b897bd9133a2daa990c5336aa94ed6a971d4d83767d5755bd5350f86c","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.974Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.974Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Practical, portable, performant digital signal processing.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/doppler-dsp/doppler/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"42b2529b897bd9133a2daa990c5336aa94ed6a971d4d83767d5755bd5350f86c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/doppler-dsp/doppler/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:05:50.975Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2